SUMMARY:Rosh Chodesh Circle Series
DESCRIPTION:Urban Adamah offers an ever-expanding calendar of community programs that integrate mind\, heart\, and body. Join us for a Shabbat celebration or other Jewish events and holidays\, a volunteer work party\, a gardening workshop\, a family farm day\, and so much more. We hope to see you on the farm soon!				\n				\n				\n				\n							\n			\n		\n						\n				\n				\n				\n									Looking for ways to bring the farm home? Looking for new ways to celebrate an upcoming holiday? Or curious about past programs offerings? Check out our virtual resource guide for various at-home gardening tips\, nature based projects for the entire family\, and programs that create spiritual connection\, and so much more! 								\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					\n						\n									Virtual Resource Guide\n					\n					\n				\n								\n				\n				\n				\n							\n			\n		\n						\n				\n				\n				\n					Filter Events By:				\n				\n				\n				\n									\n					  Youth & FamiliesFarming & NatureShabbat & HolidaysMindfulnessJewish LearningMusic & FilmRetreats		\n		\n						\n				\n					\n		\n					\n		\n					\n		\n					\n		\n				\n						\n					\n			\n						\n				\n							\n	\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						Jan 21\, 7:00pm -\n						Dec 10\, 8:30pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Rosh Chodesh Circle Series\n\n						\n											\n\n					Join us for our monthly Rosh Chodesh gatherings\, an opportunity to come together and get rooted in our Jewish tradition and the natural land cycles. Each session is crafted to correspond with the new ... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						March 29\n						4:00pm - 5:30pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Passover Family Festival\n\n						\n											\n\n					Join us on a journey through the seder\, as we celebrate Passover with a hands-on\, interactive experience for the whole family! Explore exciting stations inspired by the Haggadah\, with activities\, craf... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						April 4\n						9:30am - 6:00pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Shabbat Day-Long Mostly Silent Meditation Retreat With Adam Berman\n\n						\n											\n\n					No Previous Meditation Experience Required\n\nShabbat & Passover Day-Long Mostly Silent Meditation Retreat\nA day of stillness\, presence\, and inner freedom.\n\nAt its deepest level\, Shabbat invite... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						April 9\n						3:00pm - 5:00pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Volunteer on the Farm!\n\n						\n											\n\n					Warmer weather has arrived\, and Urban Adamah is calling on our community to come together\, tend the soil\, nurture our urban ecosystem\, and help feed both the earth and our neighbors in need.\n\nOur Fa... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						April 16\n						3:00pm - 5:00pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Volunteer on the Farm!\n\n						\n											\n\n					Warmer weather has arrived\, and Urban Adamah is calling on our community to come together\, tend the soil\, nurture our urban ecosystem\, and help feed both the earth and our neighbors in need.\n\nOur Fa... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						April 16\n						7:00pm - 8:30pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Iyar Rosh Chodesh Circle\n\n						\n											\n\n					Join us for our monthly Rosh Chodesh gatherings\, an opportunity to come together and get rooted in our Jewish tradition and the natural land cycles. Each session is crafted to correspond with the new ... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						April 19\n						11:00am - 1:00pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Death over Bagels with JADE\n\n						\n											\n\n					Join Urban Adamah and The Jewish Association for Death Education Berkeley Educator\, Yael Galinson\, for a morning of honest and engaging conversation about Jewish death practices over Boichik bagels. W... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						April 22\n						7:30pm - 8:30pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Jewish Meditation: Sitting with the Omer with R. Dorothy Richman\n\n						\n											\n\n					The seven weeks between the Jewish holidays celebrating liberation (Passover) and revelation (Shavuot) are spiritually potent and are marked by a ritual of counting each night. How can we tap into thi... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						April 23\n						3:00pm - 5:00pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Volunteer on the Farm!\n\n						\n											\n\n					Warmer weather has arrived\, and Urban Adamah is calling on our community to come together\, tend the soil\, nurture our urban ecosystem\, and help feed both the earth and our neighbors in need.\n\nOur Fa... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n			\n			\n\n				\n					\n						May 1\, 12:00am -\n						May 2\, 11:59pm\n					\n				\n\n\n\n				\n					\n						Kol: A Retreat for Jewish Music Across the Diaspora\n\n						\n											\n\n					Join us for a weekend of music making and learning\, Shabbat practices\, and community building. This unique participatory retreat brings together singers\, musicians\, and learners of diverse backgrounds... \n\n					Learn More\n				\n			\n		\n\n		\n\n	\n		\n		Next Page
